{
  "id": "ashoka",
  "title": "Ashoka",
  "description": "An illustrated map of the life of Ashoka, the Maurya emperor, from his birth at Pataliputra and the legends of Taxila, Ujjain and Vidisha, through the throne war and the conquest of Kalinga, to his edicts on rocks and pillars from Girnar to Shahbazgarhi, his pilgrimages to Bodh Gaya and Lumbini, Mahinda’s mission to Sri Lanka, the lions of Sarnath and the decipherment of his script in 1837.",
  "canvas": "geo",
  "basemap": "south-asia",
  "source": "History",
  "nativeLang": "sa",
  "routes": "chapter",
  "mapLabel": "Illustrated map of the life of Ashoka, about 304 to 232 BCE",
  "note": "Ashoka’s own edicts are the firm ground; his early life and last years come from Buddhist texts written centuries later, the Sanskrit Ashokavadana and the Sri Lankan chronicles (Dipavamsa and Mahavamsa), and those chapters are tagged Tradition. His dates are estimates. The map is stylised and not to scale; the areas under Powers are painted loosely and are not borders.",
